        "answer": {
          "short": "A Pythagorean triad.",
          "worked": "$a=9$, $b=12$, $c=15$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2+b^2&=9^2+12^2\\\\a^2+b^2&=81+144\\\\a^2+b^2&=225\\\\c^2&=15^2\\\\c^2&=225\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a^2+b^2=c^2$, the numbers form a Pythagorean triad.",
